From c3505ece7d9c5f5993caefece327243e90f83634 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): tell agents the widget hermes.send rules and
 show refused intents under the frame [daveey]

An inline rating page sent 333 ratings in one hermes.send (>500 chars).
The frame refused it as too_long and told only the page, which ignored
the ack; the page also promised localStorage saving the sandboxed frame
blocks. Every rating was lost and the user saw nothing (desktop-13785ebc41).

Root: the widget contract (500-char cap, 1/s throttle, {ok:false} ack,
no storage) lived only in a code comment, never in the agent's hint.
- PLATFORM_HINTS[desktop]: state the cap, throttle, ack/retry, chunking
  and storage ban; a test reads MAX_INTENT_LENGTH/INTENT_THROTTLE_MS from
  the renderer so the text cannot drift from the enforced limits.
- inline-preview-directive: a too_long/invalid/undelivered refusal renders
  a notice under the frame (throttled stays quiet: good widgets retry it).
